{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects tests known to fail on Windows through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/file-locks.args`. This bug owns that file: 19 tests in 15 modules. The root cause per signature, with the log evidence, is in the ticket comment \"Root cause per signature\"; in short: git's read-only objects cannot be deleted on Windows (tests); `os.replace` onto a contended target raises `PermissionError` (product, 5 tests); `src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py:62-91` `interprocess_lock`, `src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py:14-17,51-59` and the `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:355-366` guard use `fcntl` with no working Windows lock (product); one test renames a directory holding an open file; one deletes its own cwd; one rewrites git's hidden `.git` file; and one (`test_reducer_cache.py`) failed on an mtime assertion main has since replaced.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix product locks through the portable lock leg the store already uses, and make the tests stop assuming POSIX filesystem semantics where the behaviour under test does not depend on them.\n\n- Concurrent replace (5 tests: `test_unique_cache_writes.py::test_two_concurrent_writers_to_one_target_both_publish`, `test_completion_verdict_cache.py::test_concurrent_persist_for_same_criterion_loses_no_writer`, `test_plan_review.py::test_concurrent_save_checkpoint_same_digest_loses_no_writer`, `test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py::test_peer_confirmations_distinct_concurrent_saves_are_merged`, `test_mcp_gate_async.py::test_follower_start_does_not_reclobber_the_leaders_index_record`): fixed and removed from `file-locks.args` by sporting-feudalist-bluet's change. This ticket's change is pushed after that change merges and rebases onto it.\n- Locks: `interprocess_lock` takes `rebar._store.lock_kernel.take_blocking_exclusive` on the opened lock file and releases with `release_exclusive` (`src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py:120-182`, Windows `msvcrt` leg included). The `mkdir` spin fallback is removed: every supported platform has a kernel leg, and `lock_kernel` raises `NoExclusiveLegError` rather than degrade. `alert_store.append` serializes through `rebar._store.fsutil.sibling_exclusive_lock(today, lock_name=\".append.lock\")` (`src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:33-63`); retention ignores dotfiles (`src/rebar/reconciler/scratch_retention.py:84`). The janitor's non-blocking GC guard uses `lock_kernel.take_exclusive` and `is_contention`.\n- Read-only objects: clear the read-only bit (`os.chmod(p, stat.S_IWRITE | stat.S_IREAD)`) before each `unlink` at the test sites listed in the comment. In `test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py`, `shutil.rmtree(basetemp, onexc=...)` clears the bit and retries only for paths inside a `.git` directory and re-raises everything else, so the test still proves the rebar snapshot itself is removable.\n- `test_snapshot_cache.py::test_open_reader_survives_eviction_then_relookup_misses`: on Windows assert the platform's semantics, the eviction rename is refused while the reader holds the file, the reader still reads the content, and after close the entry evicts and a relookup re-heals; POSIX keeps the delete-on-last-close assertion.\n- `test_detached_child_cwd.py::test_durable_cwd_never_raises_when_the_callers_own_directory_is_gone`: `skipif(os.name == \"nt\")`, reason \"Windows refuses to delete a directory that is a process's cwd, so this state cannot occur there\".\n- `test_copied_worktree_guard.py:165`: unlink the `.git` file before writing it (git for Windows marks it hidden).\n- `test_reducer_cache.py`: remove the line; the current assertion (`:201-206`) is portable, and the sweep runs prove it.\n- Delete `file-locks.args` and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty.\n\nPortability: the new lock paths use `lock_kernel`, which selects `fcntl` or `msvcrt`; the test changes use `os.chmod` with `stat.S_IWRITE`, valid on both. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`, `src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py`, `tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py`, `tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py`, `tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py`, `tests/unit/test_snapshot_cache.py`, `tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py`, `tests/unit/store/test_copied_worktree_guard.py`\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/file-locks.args` (deleted), `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n\n## Testing\n\n- POSIX: the touched tests and the existing lock tests (`test_snapshot_cache.py` cross-process single-flight, `test_similar_tickets_index.py`, `test_alert_store_concurrency.py`, janitor GC tests) pass under `make verify`. Failure path: a held GC guard still yields `GcResult(skipped=\"locked\")` (existing janitor test).\n- Windows: 3 consecutive dispatched `sweep (windows)` runs on main after the merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The class's root cause is recorded per signature on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [x] `make verify` passes on the change.\n- [x] Every line removed from `file-locks.args` names a test that passed in 3 consecutive `sweep (windows)` runs on main after the fix (run ids recorded in a comment).\n- [x] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on those runs, with `file-locks.args` and its `@` reference removed."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795357879883526001,"uuid":"f08aeb65-7e22-4766-a1b5-976abf102988"}